{"beat": 4, "name": "THE WORLD BEFORE", "text": "Before 1913, the United States mail would carry a package of up to 4 pounds. It charged 16 cents a pound. That works out at $320 a ton. Rail freight moved the same ton for $1.90 a ton. The private express companies charged about $28 a ton. So a farm family in Kansas that wanted a stove, a plough blade, a bolt of cloth, had bad choices, all of them. Pay the mail's price, if the parcel came in under 4 pounds. Pay the express company's price. Or wait for freight, which ran to a railroad depot, not to a farm.", "provider": "placeholder", "words": [{"word": "Before", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.18}, {"word": "1913,", "start": 0.18, "end": 1.3}, {"word": "the", "start": 1.96, "end": 2.02}, {"word": "United", "start": 2.02, "end": 2.32}, {"word": "States", "start": 2.32, "end": 2.76}, {"word": "mail", "start": 2.76, "end": 3.12}, {"word": "would", "start": 3.12, "end": 3.36}, {"word": "carry", "start": 3.36, "end": 3.64}, {"word": "a", "start": 3.64, "end": 3.8}, {"word": "package", "start": 3.8, "end": 4.2}, {"word": "of", "start": 4.2, "end": 4.44}, {"word": "up", "start": 4.44, "end": 4.58}, {"word": "to", "start": 4.58, "end": 4.72}, {"word": "4", "start": 4.72, "end": 5.0}, {"word": "pounds.", "start": 5.0, "end": 5.44}, {"word": "It", "start": 6.14, "end": 6.26}, {"word": "charged", "start": 6.26, "end": 6.56}, {"word": "16", "start": 6.56, "end": 7.18}, {"word": "cents", "start": 7.18, "end": 7.48}, {"word": "a", "start": 7.48, "end": 7.68}, {"word": "pound.", "start": 7.68, "end": 8.1}, {"word": "That", "start": 8.7, "end": 8.88}, {"word": "works", "start": 8.88, "end": 9.14}, {"word": "out", "start": 9.14, "end": 9.38}, {"word": "at", "start": 9.38, "end": 9.52}, {"word": "$320", "start": 9.86, "end": 10.6}, {"word": "a", "start": 10.6, "end": 11.08}, {"word": "ton.", "start": 11.08, "end": 11.36}, {"word": "Rail", "start": 12.08, "end": 12.4}, {"word": "freight", "start": 12.4, "end": 12.7}, {"word": "moved", "start": 1